<title>FRANCE: TABLE-French May adj trade surplus 16.49 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>TABLE-French May adj trade surplus 16.49 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>France had a seasonally adjusted trade surplus of 16.485 billion francs in May compared with a revised surplus in April of 15.595 billion francs, provisional customs office data showed.</p>
<p>The office reported on July 10 a surplus in April of 23.76 billion francs.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures, in billions of francs and seasonally adjusted unless otherwise stated, were as follows:</p>
<p>					  May	April</p>
<p> Trade balance			16.49   15.60</p>
<p> Trade balance (unadjusted)     14.49   18.17</p>
<p> Imports			     118.96  121.24</p>
<p> Exports			     135.45  136.84</p>
<p> Agri-business balance	     4.95    5.98</p>
<p> Energy balance		     -5.91   -6.81</p>
<p> Industrial/military balance    13.22   12.04</p>
<p> Airbus exports	 4.45 (10 planes)   4.30(9)</p>
<p> Defence (unadj)		     1.80    1.34</p>
<p> Unadjusted exports		132.45  146.30</p>
<p> Unadjusted imports		117.96  128.13</p>
<p> European Union			6.05   10.11</p>
<p> Germany				-0.19    0.57</p>
<p> Japan				  -2.00   -1.78</p>
<p> United States			-1.62   -2.91</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 54 52</p>
</text>
